+
+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
+Compiling from source (Microsoft Windows & MSYS2 / MinGW-w64)
+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
+A MinGW-w64 Python, as MSYS2 provides it, builds PyAudio like a POSIX platform
+does: against the PortAudio package of the distribution, dynamically linked. In
+an MSYS2 UCRT64 (or MINGW64, CLANG64) shell:
+
+  $ pacman -S ${MINGW_PACKAGE_PREFIX}-{gcc,python-pip,python-setuptools,portaudio}
+  $ pip install pyaudio
+
+(CLANG64 uses ${MINGW_PACKAGE_PREFIX}-clang instead of gcc.)
